विवक्षा f. desire of saying, teaching, expressing;
meaning, sense (loc. or —˚), mere desire of saying etc., i.e.
hesitation, doubt.

विवा॑चन m. ई f. arbiter, umpire;
 n. decision,
authority.

विवत्स a. having no calf;
 bereft of the young or children
i.g.

विवध॑ m. carrying-yoke;
 burden, load, provisions,
stock of grain, etc.

वीवध m. carrying-yoke;
 burden, load, provisions, stock
of grain, etc.

विवर्जन n. abandoning, giving up;
 desisting from
(abl.).

विवर्जित a. abandoned by, destitute of, free from,
-less (instr. or —˚);
 left out —, not including (—˚).

विवर्ण a. colourless or discoloured, pale;
 abstr. ˚ता
f., ˚भाव m.

विवर्त॑ m. the turning or revolving one, i.e. the sky;
whirl-pool, eddy;
 change, altered condition;
 the mere semblance of
(—˚).

विव॑र्तन a. turning, revolving, changing;
 n. the
action of turning etc., moving hither and thither, wandering, roaming,
turning away or back;
 turning point, change.

विवर्धन f. ई (आ) increasing, strengthening,
furthering (—˚);
 n. growth, increase, welfare.

विवश a. having no will, irresolute or indolent, acting
involuntarily or against one's own will;
 abstr. ˚ता f.

वि॑वस्वन्त् a. lighting up, matutinal;
 m. N. of a god,
later E. of the sun or the god of the sun.

विव॑स्वन्त् a. lighting up, matutinal;
 m. N. of a god,
later E. of the sun or the god of the sun.

वि॑वाच् a. calling to (i.e. challenging) each other;
 f.
challenge, contest.

विवाह्य a. to be married (girl);
 fit for a matrimonial
alliance;
 related by marriage. m. son-in-law.

विविक्त a. separated, detached, isolated, single, lonely,
free from (instr. or —˚);
 clean, pure, dainty, clear, distinct;
 n.,
˚ता f. & ˚त्व n. separation, loneliness, etc.

विवृत a. uncovered, bare, open, displayed, manifested,
published, explained;
 n. adv.

विवेचन a. (f. ई) & n. discriminating, examining, or
judging (right);
 for n. also f. आ.
